From e667a9cfe10923b28d53fc9bacf82c1e42d0b7ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dan on Selwyn <dan@selwyn>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:38:43 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 25/26] net: phy: Make PHYLINK user-selectable

The symbol has no prompt, so a kernel without an in-tree MAC driver
that selects it cannot enable PHYLINK, nor SFP, which depends on it.
Out-of-tree MAC drivers then cannot use the SFP cage support. Add a
prompt; the default stays n.

Signed-off-by: TODO
---
 drivers/net/phy/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/Kconfig b/drivers/net/phy/Kconfig
index 30e9d22c8..87fa2b88a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/phy/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/Kconfig
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 #
 
 config PHYLINK
-	tristate
+	tristate "PHYlink (for out-of-tree MAC drivers)"
 	select PHYLIB
 	select SWPHY
 	help
